WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.196 --> 00:00:26.197
Brooklyn practiced with Dirk in her driveway until dark. Then someone on a bike rode past.

2
00:00:26.198 --> 00:00:30.948
"Hey, Brooklyn, want to ride to the Ice Cream Hut?" Jacey asked.

3
00:00:30.949 --> 00:00:37.035
Suddenly she noticed Dirk under the basketball hoop. "Dirk! Why are you here?"

4
00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:42.215
"I can't right now. We're practicing for tomorrow's game," Brooklyn answered.

5
00:00:42.216 --> 00:00:46.700
Dirk wiped sweat from his forehead without looking at Jacey.

6
00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:53.447
He spun around under the net and jumped up, nailing a slam dunk.

7
00:00:53.448 --> 00:00:58.189
"I can't go either," Dirk said. "I'm going to talk to Marv soon."

8
00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:05.268
Brooklyn ran to grab the ball. "Jacey, watch this cool move."

9
00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:08.250
Jacey watched Dirk for only a few seconds.

10
00:01:08.251 --> 00:01:15.677
Then she rode off on her bike without looking back. "See you guys tomorrow."

11
00:01:15.678 --> 00:01:25.576
Brooklyn arrived at the gym extra early on Saturday morning. But someone else had obviously arrived even earlier.

12
00:01:25.577 --> 00:01:33.315
A large sign hung above the spectators' section: Sit here, Brooklyn. You're no coach!

13
00:01:33.316 --> 00:01:40.719
Brooklyn gasped in surprise. Someone had gone to a lot of trouble to intimidate her.

14
00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:48.401
"That stupid sign doesn't bother me at all," she said out loud. "It just makes me more determined to win!"

15
00:01:48.402 --> 00:01:57.054
"What's that, Brooklyn?" She was ripping down the sign when Marv entered the gym.

16
00:01:57.055 --> 00:02:01.836
"Nothing." Brooklyn crumpled up the paper.

17
00:02:01.837 --> 00:02:07.128
"It's something." Marv walked closer.

18
00:02:07.129 --> 00:02:11.379
"Or you wouldn't be hiding it from me. Show it to me, please."

19
00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:18.458
She stepped off the bleachers and reluctantly spread the crumpled sign on the gym floor.

20
00:02:18.459 --> 00:02:24.273
Marv read the words and began pacing.

21
00:02:24.274 --> 00:02:27.452
"Is someone on the team bullying you?"

22
00:02:27.453 --> 00:02:33.530
"I've gotten a few messages," Brooklyn said softly. "I can handle it, Marv."

23
00:02:33.531 --> 00:02:36.867
Marv stopped pacing.

24
00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:45.258
"I believe you can handle it, Brooklyn, but that doesn't make it okay. Bullying violates our team and school rules."

25
00:02:45.259 --> 00:02:49.691
"I thought I knew who was sending me the notes, but I was wrong."

26
00:02:49.692 --> 00:02:58.200
Marv picked up the sign. "Always let people know if you're being bullied. I'll show this to the principal when she arrives.

27
00:02:58.201 --> 00:03:06.000
Right now let's prepare for the game." He started toward the gym office with the sign.

28
00:03:06.001 --> 00:03:13.406
"Please don't say anything to the players yet," Brooklyn said. "The team has to focus on the game."

29
00:03:13.407 --> 00:03:20.747
Marv smiled. "You really are a good coach, Brooklyn. You're always thinking about what's best for the team."

30
00:03:20.748 --> 00:03:31.067
Dirk was the first player to arrive. When Marv came out of the office, Dirk pumped a fist in the air. "Whales Whoosh!"

31
00:03:31.068 --> 00:03:35.573
"Whales Whoosh!" Marv said, and Brooklyn joined in.

32
00:03:35.574 --> 00:03:42.556
Noise quickly filled the gym as more players and spectators arrived.

33
00:03:42.557 --> 00:03:48.714
Brooklyn felt butterflies fluttering in her stomach. The Whales had to win today!

34
00:03:48.715 --> 00:04:02.192
In the first minute of the game, the Terriers' giant guard raced down the court and stole the ball from Jacey.

35
00:04:02.193 --> 00:04:05.955
He immediately scored.

36
00:04:05.956 --> 00:04:09.780
Jacey looked as if she might cry.

37
00:04:09.781 --> 00:04:12.765
"Shake it off, Jacey," Brooklyn called.

38
00:04:12.766 --> 00:04:16.275
Jacey glanced at Dirk, who was sitting on the bench.

39
00:04:16.276 --> 00:04:18.956
"Listen to Brooklyn!" he shouted.

40
00:04:18.957 --> 00:04:28.849
Stuart had the ball now. The referee blew his whistle. "Foul! Traveling!"

41
00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:35.459
Marv nodded at Brooklyn. Stuart was traveling, just as she had pointed out in practice.

42
00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:39.162
Seconds later Stuart had the ball again.

43
00:04:39.163 --> 00:04:48.180
"Dribble!" Brooklyn shouted. This time Stuart kept dribbling as he ran toward the net.

44
00:04:48.181 --> 00:04:56.824
He missed the shot, but Jacey grabbed the ball and sunk a basket.

45
00:04:56.825 --> 00:05:00.302
"Teamwork!" Brooklyn pumped her fist.

46
00:05:00.303 --> 00:05:11.833
Both teams raced up and down the court, scoring point after point.

47
00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:16.980
Brooklyn paced the sideline with Marv, calling to players.

48
00:05:16.981 --> 00:05:19.200
"Aaron, try a low pass!"

49
00:05:19.201 --> 00:05:20.662
"Loop it, Jacey!"

50
00:05:20.663 --> 00:05:23.060
"Way to steal, Stuart!"

51
00:05:23.061 --> 00:05:26.670
Brooklyn was pleased to see the players listening to her.

52
00:05:26.671 --> 00:05:33.141
But when she offered Jacey a cold water bottle, her friend wouldn't take it, or even look at her.

53
00:05:33.142 --> 00:05:36.212
"Great fake before that three-pointer, Jacey."

54
00:05:36.213 --> 00:05:39.457
"You're not our coach," Jacey muttered.

55
00:05:39.458 --> 00:05:49.333
The comment stung. Brooklyn swallowed, trying to keep her mind on the game instead of Jacey.

56
00:05:49.334 --> 00:05:54.528
At halftime the score was tied: 24-24.

57
00:05:54.529 --> 00:06:00.844
Marv and Brooklyn were planning plays when the Terriers coach approached.

58
00:06:00.845 --> 00:06:07.439
"I found this envelope by the Whales' cooler. Belong to anybody on the team?"

59
00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:10.511
Brooklyn's name was on the front of the envelope.

60
00:06:10.512 --> 00:06:18.934
She opened it, her hands shaking, and read the note inside: You'll always be a clumsy loser.

61
00:06:18.935 --> 00:06:26.086
So far Brooklyn hadn't let the notes bother her. But this one made tears spring to her eyes.

62
00:06:26.087 --> 00:06:32.601
Marv gave her his handkerchief. "Don't worry. It's clean," he joked softly.

63
00:06:32.602 --> 00:06:41.307
He led her to the team bench. "Take slow, deep breaths. After the game I'm showing this note to the principal too.

64
00:06:41.308 --> 00:06:47.076
The bully will be punished. But right now, kid, I need your coaching help."

65
00:06:47.077 --> 00:06:49.632
Brooklyn sniffled and nodded.

66
00:06:49.633 --> 00:06:54.147
Marv waved over the players. "Gather round, Whales."

67
00:06:54.148 --> 00:06:58.802
Aaron saw Brooklyn wiping her eyes. "What's wrong?"

68
00:06:58.803 --> 00:07:03.608
"It looks like someone on our team is bullying Brooklyn," Marv said.

69
00:07:03.609 --> 00:07:06.566
"Huh?" a few players said.

70
00:07:06.567 --> 00:07:14.875
"Is this about those messages?" Jacey asked. "Brooklyn, maybe you shouldn't coach us today if you're really upset."

71
00:07:14.876 --> 00:07:19.372
Dirk gave Jacey a look. "Brooklyn is helping our team."

72
00:07:19.373 --> 00:07:25.045
"Yeah," said Stuart. "She knew when I had an opening to steal in the second quarter."

73
00:07:25.046 --> 00:07:28.946
"Her tips totally helped my dribbling," said Aaron.

74
00:07:28.947 --> 00:07:33.705
"Marv has a lot more experience," Jacey said sharply.

75
00:07:33.706 --> 00:07:36.046
Brooklyn's tears had dried.

76
00:07:36.047 --> 00:07:44.375
She suddenly pictured Jacey on her bike yesterday . . . Jacey's frown when Brooklyn and Dirk didn't stop practicing to go to the Ice Cream Hut.

77
00:07:44.376 --> 00:07:47.178
Was Jacey jealous?

78
00:07:47.179 --> 00:07:51.588
"Brooklyn will stay and help me," Marv said sternly.

79
00:07:51.589 --> 00:07:54.927
"But Jacey, you can leave right now.

80
00:07:54.928 --> 00:08:00.591
In fact, maybe you'd like to go talk to the principal about that sign you made."

81
00:08:00.592 --> 00:08:07.185
Jacey's mouth opened and shut, like a goldfish out of its bowl gasping in the air.

82
00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:14.930
Brooklyn had guessed at the same time as Marv. "Did you write those notes to me?" she blurted out.

83
00:08:14.931 --> 00:08:21.318
Jacey didn't answer. She just ran out of the gym.

84
00:08:21.319 --> 00:08:26.155
The buzzer sounded to start the second half.

85
00:08:26.156 --> 00:08:29.169
"Play smart, Whales!" Marv said.

86
00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:36.002
Brooklyn stood, her legs wobbling. Jacey was her friend. How could she . . .?

87
00:08:36.003 --> 00:08:42.826
"Focus!" Brooklyn told herself fiercely. "That's what coaches do!"

88
00:08:42.827 --> 00:08:46.897
The Whales and Terriers continued battling for points.

89
00:08:46.898 --> 00:08:57.961
With forty seconds left on the clock, Dirk whipped around under the net to slam-dunk a shot and tie up the game.

90
00:08:57.962 --> 00:09:08.026
The next time Aaron had the ball, the frustrated Terriers' giant fouled, bumping hard into Aaron.

91
00:09:08.027 --> 00:09:12.721
Now the Whales had a free throw they could take the lead!

92
00:09:12.722 --> 00:09:21.962
Aaron stepped up for the shot—and missed. Brooklyn groaned.

93
00:09:21.963 --> 00:09:29.252
The clock ticked down to twenty seconds as a Terrier raced downcourt with the ball.

94
00:09:29.253 --> 00:09:31.360
Dirk signaled Stuart.

95
00:09:31.361 --> 00:09:35.612
"Yes!" Brooklyn whispered. "It's time to try it!"

96
00:09:35.613 --> 00:09:46.784
She hoped her practice with Dirk the Jedi would pay off before the final buzzer.
